index 0000000..9e0eb73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/storage/droppedseriesnames/CODEMANIFEST
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+Usages:
+  fill_until_full_no_eviction: |
+    Like its sibling metricnamestats, DroppedSeriesTracker never evicts individual entries once
+    the configured byte budget is reached: cacheIsFull checks currentSizeBytes against
+    maxSizeBytes and, once exceeded, IncrementDropCount becomes a silent no-op for any metric
+    name not already tracked — existing entries keep being incremented forever until an
+    explicit Reset clears the whole map. store is a flat map[string]*atomic.Uint64 with counter
+    and metric-name allocations bump-batched (counterBuf/metricNamesBuf, reset together in
+    initEmpty), the same batching idea metricnamestats and metricsmetadata each use for their
+    own per-entry allocations.
+
+    Unlike metricnamestats, this cell holds no tenant dimension (no accountID/projectID) and no
+    on-disk persistence: state is reset to empty on every process restart, matching the
+    lifecycle of the aggregate HourlySeriesLimitRowsDropped/DailySeriesLimitRowsDropped counters
+    it complements in lib/storage.
+
+Annotations: |
+  In-memory, bounded tracker of, per metric name, how many samples were dropped because adding
+  that series would have exceeded a configured hourly or daily unique-series cardinality limit
+  (lib/storage's -storage.maxHourlySeries / -storage.maxDailySeries) — the data backing
+  support's "which metric names hit our series limit" question, surfaced via TopRecords. All
+  exported DroppedSeriesTracker methods tolerate a nil receiver as a no-op, so an owning cell
+  may hold a `DroppedSeriesTracker` field that is intentionally left nil (e.g. the feature
+  disabled, or neither limiter configured) without a nil-check at every call site.
+
+  Use `fill_until_full_no_eviction` before changing IncrementDropCount, cacheIsFull, or Reset —
+  this cell's cache-fullness policy and lack of persistence are intentional, not oversights.
+
+---
+
+"DroppedSeriesTracker(maxSizeBytes: uint64)":
+  location: tracker.go
+  annotations: |
+    Obtained via the NewTracker factory function. `maxSizeBytes` bounds total tracked-entry
+    size; a value of 0 falls back to DefaultMaxSizeBytes. See `fill_until_full_no_eviction` for
+    what happens once the budget is reached.
+  methods:
+    "IncrementDropCount(metricName: []byte)": |
+      Record one dropped sample for `metricName`, creating a new zero-based counter for it if
+      one does not already exist. No-ops once the cache is full — see
+      `fill_until_full_no_eviction`. Nil-safe.
+    "TopRecords(limit: int) -> result:DroppedSeriesStatsResult": |
+      Return at most `limit` tracked metric names with the highest DroppedRowsCount, sorted in
+      descending order (ties broken by MetricName ascending), together with tracker-wide
+      totals. A negative `limit` returns every tracked record. Nil-safe.
+    "IsEmpty() -> isEmpty:bool": |
+      Report whether any entries are currently tracked. Nil-safe.
+    "Reset()": |
+      Clear all tracked entries and restart the collection window returned as
+      DroppedSeriesStatsResult's collectedSinceTs property. Nil-safe.
+    "UpdateMetrics(dst: DroppedSeriesTrackerMetrics)": |
+      Populate `dst` with the current tracked-item count, byte size, and configured
+      maxSizeBytes. Nil-safe.
+
+"DroppedSeriesStatsResult(collectedSinceTs: uint64, trackedNames: uint64, maxSizeBytes: uint64, currentSizeBytes: uint64, records: []Record)":
+  location: tracker.go
+  annotations: |
+    Response payload for a TopRecords call: the matched `Record`s plus the tracker-wide totals
+    (irrespective of any limit the call requested) as of the call.
+
+"Record(metricName: string, droppedRowsCount: uint64)":
+  location: tracker.go
+  annotations: |
+    One tracked metric name's dropped-samples count, as surfaced to a caller.
+
+"DroppedSeriesTrackerMetrics(currentSizeBytes: uint64, currentItemsCount: uint64, maxSizeBytes: uint64)":
+  location: tracker.go
+  annotations: |
+    Plain snapshot struct populated by DroppedSeriesTracker's UpdateMetrics method; carries no
+    behavior of its own.
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 21/09/26
+Description: |
+  In-memory, bounded, non-persisted, non-tenant-aware tracker of per-metric-name dropped-sample
+  counts caused by lib/storage's hourly/daily series cardinality limiters, with the same
+  fill-until-full (no per-entry eviction) cache-fullness policy as the sibling metricnamestats
+  cell — see `fill_until_full_no_eviction`. Added as a new nested Goga cell under lib/storage so
+  that support engineers can answer "which metric names hit our series limit" without asking
+  customers to dig through their own instrumentation. Consumed directly by lib/storage, which
+  feeds it from the two series-cardinality-limiter reject branches inside AddRows.
